 While the root-scoped `conversation.session.header.views.actions` list has registrations, a **More conversation views** button with a tooltip follows the View tabs in the tab row. It opens a menu whose rows are that list's registrations. Each receives `entries` (Views outside the header in registration order with `id`, `label`, `pinned`, and `active`; Chat is never listed), `onOpen(id)`, which selects the View in this Session, `onPinnedChange(id, pinned)`, and `onDismiss()`, which closes the menu. The header keeps an in-memory list of unpinned View ids shared by every Session; the tab bar omits unpinned Views and places registered Chat first so it always remains outside More. Plugin reload resets pin choices, and legacy localStorage values are ignored. The tab bar's visibility counts available Views, not pinned ones, so the bar and More stay while every other View is unpinned. Unpinning the active View hides its tab immediately without changing the selected content. More lists only Views outside the header and identifies the current View through `active`. The header reads its available row width, reserves 48px for More and padding, and estimates 120px per tab. Remaining Views keep registration order in More. A single ResizeObserver watches the tab row so window resizing and sidebar expansion update the split; active selection does not change the order. The observer disconnects when the row is removed. If ResizeObserver is unavailable, the initial width calculation still applies without subsequent observation. The More button highlights and names the active View in its tooltip when that View is folded. Individual tabs are not measured. At least one preferred tab remains outside, and long labels truncate with a full-name tooltip. Unregistered View ids remain in the in-memory pin list until plugin reload.
 
 The composer registers the File command action and owns its label, availability, and native file-dialog callback. Menu availability and invocation both consult the mounted composer's current attachment-intake policy. Unmounting or locking the composer disables that action; disposing the plugin removes its registration. The callback binding stays inside the input module.
+
+`IConversation.addDraftFiles(files)` is available only through a Session-scoped Conversation service. It registers browser-owned File objects in that Session's composer draft, starts the existing background upload for generic files, and refuses a locked/busy input without sending. The caller retains responsibility for identifying and authorizing the source file; the service does not accept URLs or fetch remote resources.
 
 `SessionInputShell` owns one Lexical editor per Session through its private [DraftEditorRuntime](src/client/input/editor/runtime.ts), while retaining submission, attachment selection, and recovery decisions. [DraftEditor](src/client/input/editor/DraftEditor.tsx) renders the borrowed editor; InputBar retains its Hooks and refs and installs DOM behavior through [view-binding](src/client/input/editor/view-binding.ts). Editor-facing types live in [draft-editor.ts](src/client/contract/draft-editor.ts), with shared input and submission types in [input.ts](src/client/contract/input.ts). Background editor updates retain the draft selection without changing the document selection or reclaiming focus from another control; explicit Composer focus restores its selection. This separation does not support simultaneous editable roots for one Session; [the two-stage isolation proposal](../../../.agents/notes/proposed/architecture/2026-09-14-composer-model-and-draft-editor.md) defines the remaining work.
 
